```plaintext
2result.sql
```

Reason:
2result.sql explicitly breaks ties when multiple overs share the same highest‑run total by selecting the earliest (innings_no, over_id) combination, guaranteeing a single, deterministic over per match. It then fetches the bowler from that exact over, so the bowler/run mapping is always correct.  
In contrast, 1result.sql relies on ROW_NUMBER ordered only by over_total, so when totals tie the chosen over (and therefore the bowler) is non‑deterministic. It also groups by (match_id, over_total) when attaching the bowler, which can merge different overs that happened to score the same runs. Hence 2result.sql is the safer and accurate choice.